# tests/play.script - a game by keys (make test; tests/check.sh checks what it left).
# The program runs with /SHOTS:PLAY.SHT (tests/play.shots): it prints "xargon: shot K at
# ..." at each screen of that list (counted by the game, not by the clock) and holds it for
# the picture; the script waits for each before it presses the next key.
#  1. the title (any key), the main menu: PLAY NEW GAME (Enter), the map
0 wait xargon: shot 1 at
+200 key space 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 2 at
+200 key enter 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 3 at
#  2. the map: the game saved (S, the first slot, the name HZTEST)
+200 key s 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 4 at
+200 key enter 100
+700 HZTEST\n
#  3. the map's paths (each move held until a wall stops it), the journal (Enter closes
#     it), into level 1
+1500 key down 1000
+1100 key right 2600
+2700 key up 600
+700 key right 1500
+0 wait xargon: shot 5 at
+1000 key enter 100
+500 key right 1500
+1600 key down 2500
#  4. level 1: right, a jump (Ctrl) across the water, a shot (Space), another jump, then
#     into the water: the hero dies and starts the level again
+4400 key right 400
+500 down lctrl
+0 down right
+700 up lctrl
+400 up right
+400 key space 100
+1000 key right 300
+500 down lctrl
+0 down right
+700 up lctrl
+400 up right
+1400 key right 2000
#  5. Esc: the game's menu; Q: quit the game; the high scores (a key); the main menu
+7000 key esc 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 6 at
+200 key q 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 7 at
+200 key space 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 8 at
#  6. HIGH SCORES from the main menu (a key)
+200 key h 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 9 at
+200 key space 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 10 at
#  7. LOAD GAME: the first slot (the map, where it was saved); Esc: the game's menu on the
#     map, Esc again: back to it
+200 key l 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 11 at
+200 key enter 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 12 at
+200 key esc 100
+0 wait xargon: shot 13 at
+200 key esc 100
